        "title": "refactor: consolidate bounded concurrency on p-limit and p-map",
        "body": "Closes #105971\n\nAI-assisted: yes. The implementation was produced with Codex and reviewed with the repository autoreview workflow.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nResolves a maintenance and correctness problem where multiple core, package, plugin, and tooling paths independently implemented bounded-concurrency worker loops with subtly different scheduling and error behavior.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nUses `p-limit` and `p-map` at their owning dependency boundaries, with explicit stop-on-error or continue-on-error handling at each call site. Specialized weighted, abort-aware, lifecycle, and early-stop schedulers remain custom because their contracts are not generic bounded mapping.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo intentional user-visible behavior change. Embeddings, media uploads, model scanning, plugin workflows, and repository tooling keep their existing ordering, progress, and error semantics with less bespoke concurrency code.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Exact-head Testbox focused concurrency suite: 21 files / 354 tests passed.\n- Exact-head `pnpm test:changed`: 11 shards passed, including 5,988 tooling tests plus all touched runtime/plugin suites.\n- Exact-head memory host SDK test: 11/11 passed, including stop-and-drain failure behavior.\n- Exact-head `pnpm build`: passed, including plugin SDK export verification and Control UI build.\n- Targeted shrinkwrap checks passed for all owned package/plugin lockfiles; the broader shrinkwrap lane passed all 76 checks.\n- Fresh autoreview found two real issues across its iterations: the public memory-host concurrency re-export was restored, and memory-host failures now stop scheduling while draining in-flight writes. Both fixes have regression proof; the final whole-branch review is clean.\n- `git diff --check`: passed.\n- Diff is LOC-negative: 611 additions / 790 deletions (net -179).\n\nKnown baseline-only gaps: the broad changed gate reaches repository-wide TypeScript LOC and plugin-SDK surface ratchets that are independently red on current `main`. All touched over-baseline files shrink or meet their baseline; exact-head tests, build, dependency/shrinkwrap checks, and focused surface proof pass.\n",
